      },
      "message": "Merge main into issue/889-camtools-holder-body (tool_import.rs and 3 more: holder bodies ride on #899's ImportMode)\n\nImportTools keeps #899's ImportMode (Add/Update/Replace), its Step plan\nand change_refusal gates intact; the #889 holders choice becomes the\nfourth parameter of ImportTools::with_options (with_mode = holders on,\nwith_holders = Add). In Update/Replace a file body that differs from the\ndocument tool's is a Step::Change like any other: it passes\nchange_refusal (which fits the body that will stand) and the body digest\nin the op stamp stales the operations using the tool, exactly as\nSetToolBody does; undo restores the old body. Holders off, or a bodyless\nentry, leaves the document body as it is (never cleared silently), and\nthat body must fit the incoming record. Every file body is still fitted\nat command creation.\n\nMCP import_tool_library takes both mode and holders; cam.importTools is\n(path, mode?, holders?) with cam.d.ts regenerated; the Tool library page\nkeeps the mode combo and the \"Import tool holders\" checkbox. #1060's\ntool_import_modes builds its LibraryTool with LibraryTool::bare (the\nstruct gained `body`). camcraft-mcp skill doc names both arguments;\nPROCESS_VERSION 19 (main's 18 + 1). Decision file updated (item 8).\n\nPinned: tool_library_holders every_mode_round_trips_the_bodies_and_\nholders_off_lands_bare, update_and_replace_take_a_changed_body_in_place_\nand_stale_the_op_as_set_tool_body_does, a_changed_body_in_update_and_\nreplace_takes_the_change_gates.\n\nRefs #889\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
